1
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:11,533
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:32,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,900
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,733 --> 00:00:40,800
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:43,567
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:44,667
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,300
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:47,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:50,900
<i> Stop!</i>

10
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,200
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,167
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:57,367
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,333 --> 00:00:59,867
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:02,633
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:05,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,967 --> 00:01:09,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,333
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:12,867
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,567 --> 00:01:20,900
<i> The court's issuing an order</i>

21
00:01:21,033 --> 00:01:23,767
<i>to transfer Victor Zafra
to maximum security.</i>

22
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,033
<i> This is our best chance.</i>

23
00:01:25,167 --> 00:01:26,600
I'll bring your son home later.

24
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:28,433
<i>Remember, there'll be
no unauthorized stops.</i>

25
00:01:28,567 --> 00:01:29,667
<i> No matter what happens,</i>

26
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:31,567
<i>we need to get him into
maximum security detention.</i>

27
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,800
<i> Block them!</i>

28
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:34,333
<i> Chase them down!</i>

29
00:01:34,467 --> 00:01:35,967
<i> Go on, secure Zafra!</i>

30
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,867
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

31
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:39,900
<i> Papa, let's go!</i>

32
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:41,233
<i> More of them are showing up!</i>

33
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:42,533
<i> This is where you'll rot.</i>

34
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:44,000
[INMATES SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY]

35
00:01:44,133 --> 00:01:45,300
<i> Betchay's awake.</i>

36
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:48,300
<i>Your Auntie Mameng hid her
in the bathroom.</i>

37
00:01:48,433 --> 00:01:50,733
<i>Why are you rushing me
out of the house?</i>

38
00:01:50,867 --> 00:01:53,133
<i>Why does it seem like
she hates you?</i>

39
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:55,900
<i>I will never forget
what you did to me.</i>

40
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:58,267
<i>And you can never
bring my baby back.</i>

41
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,467
<i>I didn't mean for
my sibling to die.</i>

42
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:01,733
<i> That makes two of us.</i>

43
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:16,267
- Empoy.
- Hey, Ipe!

44
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,500
Ipe.

45
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:21,267
Gabo has a message.

46
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,933
Tell all the guys.

47
00:02:23,667 --> 00:02:25,833
Keep an eye on every alley
here in Paraiso.

48
00:02:25,967 --> 00:02:28,533
Watch closely for any
new faces coming in.

49
00:02:28,667 --> 00:02:30,433
If you notice anyone suspicious,

50
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:31,933
and they're not from
around here,

51
00:02:32,067 --> 00:02:33,667
let us know right away.
Or tell Gabo.

52
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,567
Sure, you can count on us,
right?

53
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,967
- Yeah.
- We'll take care of it.

54
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:38,367
- Okay.
- Let's tell the others.

55
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:39,567
Spread out! Spread out!

56
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:40,933
- Let's go!
- Let's tell the others.

57
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:42,400
- [RUDY] It won't budge.
- Dante!

58
00:02:42,533 --> 00:02:43,933
What?

59
00:02:44,067 --> 00:02:47,400
Here. Pick out a
replacement roof now.

60
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:49,467
If we fix it today,

61
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:51,533
Betchay might start
nagging again.

62
00:02:51,667 --> 00:02:53,633
[ELTON CHUCKLES]

63
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:56,400
You know, the moment
Betchay woke up earlier,

64
00:02:56,533 --> 00:02:59,367
she immediately started
nagging Rudy over breakfast.

65
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:00,600
[BADONG] Yeah, Miss Mameng.

66
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:02,433
We could hear her loud
and clear from here.

67
00:03:02,567 --> 00:03:04,433
Let her be bothered
by the noise.

68
00:03:04,567 --> 00:03:05,900
What are you talking about?

69
00:03:06,033 --> 00:03:08,000
Gabo already talked to her.

70
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:09,833
He gave her money.

71
00:03:10,467 --> 00:03:13,900
Once that money hit her hand,

72
00:03:14,033 --> 00:03:16,033
she came to her senses.

73
00:03:16,167 --> 00:03:18,133
So don't get her
riled up anymore.

74
00:03:18,267 --> 00:03:19,867
Just sweet-talk her
a little, okay?

75
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,167
After she made it clear
that I'm useless?

76
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:23,700
And I'm supposed to
sweet-talk her?

77
00:03:23,833 --> 00:03:25,333
Why don't you just
put up with her?

78
00:03:25,467 --> 00:03:28,100
You know the situation,
don't you?

79
00:03:28,233 --> 00:03:29,667
If she changes her mind,

80
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,533
we'll be the ones in trouble.

81
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:33,967
Are you okay here?

82
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,533
I'm sorry about our...

83
00:03:37,167 --> 00:03:38,367
...room, okay?

84
00:03:39,033 --> 00:03:40,633
[GABO] It's small, but...

85
00:03:41,067 --> 00:03:42,200
...it's okay, right?

86
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:45,033
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

87
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:46,733
[BETCHAY] Who's he talking to?

88
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:49,767
- Hide!
- Oh!

89
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,567
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

90
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:54,167
Hide!

91
00:03:54,633 --> 00:03:55,700
Don't make a sound!

92
00:03:55,833 --> 00:03:57,833
- She might hear us.
- Why are we hiding?

93
00:03:57,967 --> 00:03:59,000
Shh!

94
00:03:59,767 --> 00:04:06,767
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:04:08,200 --> 00:04:09,267
[RUDY] Betchay. Betchay!

96
00:04:09,767 --> 00:04:10,800
Betchay!

97
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:13,000
Uh, you're leaving?

98
00:04:13,533 --> 00:04:15,333
Of course.
I'm already dressed.

99
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:16,600
What?

100
00:04:16,733 --> 00:04:18,400
Are you going to stop me again?

101
00:04:18,533 --> 00:04:20,100
Are you going to
lecture me again?

102
00:04:20,233 --> 00:04:21,467
I'm sorry, okay?

103
00:04:21,933 --> 00:04:24,100
The truth is,
I'm just worried about you.

104
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:27,500
You know how cunning
Paquito is.

105
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:29,833
And besides...

106
00:04:30,367 --> 00:04:31,600
doesn't he like you?

107
00:04:31,733 --> 00:04:33,533
So what if he likes me?

108
00:04:35,033 --> 00:04:36,267
Are you jealous?

109
00:04:38,767 --> 00:04:39,867
Fine.

110
00:04:40,367 --> 00:04:42,700
Think whatever you want.

111
00:04:43,733 --> 00:04:45,367
But as far as I'm concerned,

112
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,233
I don't trust him.

113
00:04:47,367 --> 00:04:49,467
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

114
00:04:49,967 --> 00:04:51,533
It's just work, Rudy.

115
00:04:52,233 --> 00:04:54,333
And if I were going to
entertain Paquito,

116
00:04:54,467 --> 00:04:56,233
I would've done it by now.

117
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,267
Besides, I'm not going to
let Paquito fool me.

118
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,700
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

119
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:06,300
Okay, how about this?

120
00:05:08,733 --> 00:05:11,400
If I can't stop you...

121
00:05:11,533 --> 00:05:14,700
just promise me
you'll be careful.

122
00:05:14,833 --> 00:05:17,233
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

123
00:05:17,367 --> 00:05:20,467
[BETCHAY] So he really does
still care about me.

124
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,700
Don't worry. I'll be careful.

125
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,600
[WHISPERS] I'm all yours.

126
00:05:32,067 --> 00:05:37,133
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

127
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:41,000
Don't make a sound!
She might hear us.

128
00:05:41,133 --> 00:05:43,000
- Why are we hiding?
- Shh!

129
00:05:43,967 --> 00:05:45,167
Don't make a sound!

130
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,500
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

131
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,833
She might come in here later.

132
00:05:52,833 --> 00:05:54,100
Don't worry.

133
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:55,767
She won't come in here.

134
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:57,133
She's mad at me.

135
00:05:59,267 --> 00:06:00,867
Then why are we hiding?

136
00:06:01,133 --> 00:06:02,633
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

137
00:06:02,767 --> 00:06:04,900
Uh, just in case
she suddenly comes in.

138
00:06:05,033 --> 00:06:06,200
I'm scared.

139
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:08,333
Wait a second. Are you...

140
00:06:08,467 --> 00:06:10,167
Are you making a move
on me?

141
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,633
Huh?

142
00:06:11,767 --> 00:06:13,933
Why would I make a move on you?

143
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:15,333
Aren't we married?

144
00:06:18,233 --> 00:06:19,267
Oh.

145
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,500
That's right.

146
00:06:20,633 --> 00:06:25,467
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

147
00:06:26,267 --> 00:06:27,667
I'm scared.

148
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,733
What if Auntie Betchay
suddenly comes in?

149
00:06:29,867 --> 00:06:31,667
Shh. Don't say anything.

150
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:36,367
Can you hug me
so I won't be scared?

151
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:37,567
Shh!

152
00:06:38,167 --> 00:06:39,133
[GABO] Come on.

153
00:06:39,267 --> 00:06:40,500
Your Auntie Betchay
already left!

154
00:06:40,633 --> 00:06:41,800
What are you doing?!

155
00:06:42,467 --> 00:06:44,533
Oh, no! Papa!

156
00:06:44,667 --> 00:06:46,533
We weren't doing anything!

157
00:06:47,133 --> 00:06:48,833
We just covered ourselves
with a blanket

158
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:50,667
because Auntie Betchay
might suddenly come in.

159
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:53,433
If she sees Gloria,
she'll definitely get mad.

160
00:06:53,567 --> 00:06:56,067
Sorry for interrupting
you two, okay?

161
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,533
No, Pa. It's okay.

162
00:06:58,667 --> 00:07:01,633
Oh, Gloria, I'm sorry, okay?

163
00:07:02,367 --> 00:07:05,967
Betchay's mind
is all over the place.

164
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,700
She thinks differently.

165
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:09,433
She really confuses us
sometimes.

166
00:07:09,567 --> 00:07:12,033
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] It's okay.

167
00:07:12,167 --> 00:07:14,867
Uh, Pa.

168
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:18,667
Maybe we should just
have the roof fixed.

169
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:21,867
It might rain tonight,
and our house might get flooded.

170
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,333
You're right. We should.

171
00:07:23,467 --> 00:07:25,900
Go see Elton, Badong,
and Dante.

172
00:07:26,033 --> 00:07:27,333
Tell them, okay? Go on.

173
00:07:27,467 --> 00:07:29,500
Honey, I'm just going outside

174
00:07:29,967 --> 00:07:31,433
so we can get this roof fixed.

175
00:07:31,567 --> 00:07:37,233
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

176
00:07:41,367 --> 00:07:43,967
- Sir Elton, Sir Badong.
- Yes, Gabo?

177
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:46,433
Papa said maybe we can
work on the roof now.

178
00:07:46,567 --> 00:07:47,533
Oh, yeah, Gabo.

179
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,633
Miss Mameng already
told us earlier.

180
00:07:49,767 --> 00:07:51,333
She even told Dante

181
00:07:51,467 --> 00:07:53,733
to buy the materials
we'll need.

182
00:07:54,367 --> 00:07:56,933
Gabo, you're pretty lucky
with your wife, huh?

183
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,600
She's so fair and beautiful.

184
00:07:59,733 --> 00:08:01,533
Where did you manage
to land her?

185
00:08:02,233 --> 00:08:03,533
We met at...

186
00:08:04,967 --> 00:08:07,133
We met at the prison.

187
00:08:07,267 --> 00:08:08,567
At the prison?

188
00:08:09,033 --> 00:08:10,967
You'd never know
by looking at her.

189
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,467
She's so beautiful.

190
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:15,033
I was just surprised to hear
she's an ex-convict.

191
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,600
Mang Elton, you can't tell
by looking at someone

192
00:08:18,733 --> 00:08:20,400
whether they'll do
something bad or not.

193
00:08:20,533 --> 00:08:23,733
Sometimes, the ones who
look beautiful and innocent

194
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:27,200
are the ones who commit
crimes you'd never expect.

195
00:08:27,333 --> 00:08:28,267
That's true.

196
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,033
But, Gabo, just a reminder,
okay?

197
00:08:31,167 --> 00:08:32,333
Be very cautious.

198
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:34,067
Be good.

199
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:37,633
Who knows one day she'd be gone.

200
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:39,400
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

201
00:08:39,533 --> 00:08:40,933
Don't worry, Elton.

202
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:43,333
Gloria is a kind person.

203
00:08:43,467 --> 00:08:44,733
I know her very well.

204
00:08:44,867 --> 00:08:45,967
She does look kind.

205
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:49,033
Hey, what's this about?

206
00:08:49,167 --> 00:08:51,333
- It's nothing.
- Oh, Mameng.

207
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:54,333
We're just talking
about Gabo's beautiful wife.

208
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,700
For what reason?

209
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:58,067
Don't talk about her, will you?

210
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,767
She's a kind woman.

211
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:02,667
Oh, you men
are really something else.

212
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:05,467
Quit gossiping!

213
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,133
- It's not like that, Mameng.
- Don't deny it!

214
00:09:07,267 --> 00:09:09,100
- Mameng!
- I could hear you...

215
00:09:09,233 --> 00:09:10,267
- Oh, Dante.
- Mameng.

216
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:12,500
Here are the materials.

217
00:09:12,633 --> 00:09:14,300
They should start repairing
the roof now.

218
00:09:14,433 --> 00:09:16,067
- Oh, that's good.
- See?

219
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:18,800
Gloria.

220
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:19,967
Don't worry.

221
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,867
My son is a good man.

222
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,967
Honestly, I think
you're very lucky.

223
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,333
He's really a responsible man.

224
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,800
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:09:30,033 --> 00:09:31,767
I'm so sorry,

226
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:34,933
but I don't really
remember anything, so...

227
00:09:35,067 --> 00:09:36,967
I can't remember what he's like.

228
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:38,133
Is that so?

229
00:09:38,267 --> 00:09:40,200
But don't worry.

230
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:42,233
We'll help you get to know him.

231
00:09:42,967 --> 00:09:44,400
And remember who you are.

232
00:09:45,467 --> 00:09:47,867
And I can assure you

233
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,267
that you are safe in our home.

234
00:09:51,033 --> 00:09:52,200
I'll just be outside.

235
00:09:52,333 --> 00:09:53,467
I'll help take care of things.

236
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,800
- Okay.
- Talk to you later.

237
00:09:54,933 --> 00:09:55,900
Thanks.

238
00:09:56,033 --> 00:09:56,900
Okay.

239
00:09:57,033 --> 00:09:58,233
[MUSIC FADES]

240
00:09:58,367 --> 00:10:00,333
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:10:00,467 --> 00:10:02,033
<i> All of them seem kind.</i>

242
00:10:03,567 --> 00:10:05,700
<i>But I still
shouldn't trust them.</i>

243
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:09,667
<i> These people are criminals.</i>

244
00:10:10,433 --> 00:10:11,867
<i> They're good at pretending.</i>

245
00:10:13,133 --> 00:10:15,300
<i>If they think
I believe their lies...</i>

246
00:10:16,267 --> 00:10:17,400
<i> they're wrong.</i>

247
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,833
<i>I'm the one
making a fool out of them.</i>

248
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:23,900
<i> I won't be here long.</i>

249
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:29,267
<i>I'll soon find out
their connection</i>

250
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:32,167
<i> with Mr. Chan and the Zafras.</i>

251
00:10:39,767 --> 00:10:41,033
- Oh.
- Rudy.

252
00:10:41,033 --> 00:10:42,867
- Pa.
- Are these for the repair?

253
00:10:42,867 --> 00:10:44,667
- Yes.
- Here.

254
00:10:44,667 --> 00:10:46,867
They've gotten expensive.
The prices doubled.

255
00:10:46,867 --> 00:10:48,333
What can we do?

256
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:49,767
Everything's getting pricier.

257
00:10:49,767 --> 00:10:51,733
- Oh, Rudy.
- [RUDY] What?

258
00:10:51,733 --> 00:10:52,833
We'll be at the back.

259
00:10:52,833 --> 00:10:54,533
Bring the hammer.

260
00:10:54,533 --> 00:10:57,400
- And this one.
- And the saw.

261
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,967
Be careful, okay?

262
00:10:58,967 --> 00:11:00,067
Gabo.

263
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:02,733
I think your wife
should stay outside.

264
00:11:02,733 --> 00:11:04,433
Debris might fall
while they're doing the repairs.

265
00:11:04,433 --> 00:11:05,600
Alright, Pa.

266
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:06,800
Okay.

267
00:11:08,667 --> 00:11:12,167
Uh, love, I think
we should stay outside.

268
00:11:12,167 --> 00:11:13,300
They'll be repairing the roof.

269
00:11:13,933 --> 00:11:15,667
- Uh, sure.
- Come on.

270
00:11:17,967 --> 00:11:19,667
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:11:19,667 --> 00:11:20,600
Come on.

272
00:11:22,233 --> 00:11:23,400
[SCREEN DOOR RATTLES]

273
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,767
[GABO] Let's stay here for now.

274
00:11:30,433 --> 00:11:31,500
- Auntie.
- Yes?

275
00:11:32,167 --> 00:11:33,100
Oh.

276
00:11:33,667 --> 00:11:34,767
Oh, Gabo.

277
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:39,367
Why don't you buy her
nice clothes?

278
00:11:39,367 --> 00:11:41,433
There's a thrift store
near the wet market.

279
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:42,800
They have a nice selection.

280
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:46,400
Oh, there's no need for that.
I'm fine borrowing his clothes.

281
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:48,833
You should have your own stuff.

282
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:52,400
You can't just borrow his stuff
all the time.

283
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,033
That's not enough.

284
00:11:54,033 --> 00:11:55,933
You're really asking Gabo
to shop for her?

285
00:11:55,933 --> 00:11:57,900
He doesn't know anything
about women's clothes.

286
00:11:57,900 --> 00:11:59,533
Oh, it's okay, Pa.

287
00:11:59,533 --> 00:12:03,533
Trust me,
I have great taste in clothes.

288
00:12:03,533 --> 00:12:05,333
Especially if it's for my wife.

289
00:12:06,333 --> 00:12:10,133
Fine then. Go and buy snacks
for Elton and Badong too.

290
00:12:13,267 --> 00:12:16,333
- Okay. I got it.
- Okay.

291
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:20,733
Love, I'll just buy food
for Uncle Elton.

292
00:12:20,733 --> 00:12:21,800
Do you want something?

293
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,200
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY] No, I'm good.

294
00:12:24,067 --> 00:12:25,600
Okay, I'll be back in a bit.

295
00:12:26,633 --> 00:12:28,033
- I'll get going, Pa.
- Okay.

296
00:12:29,433 --> 00:12:31,100
- Come, let's sit.
- Yeah.

297
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:34,267
Come, dear. Let's sit here.

298
00:12:34,267 --> 00:12:35,733
Maybe you still feel tired.

299
00:12:36,667 --> 00:12:40,200
I'm sorry about our humble home.

300
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:43,967
It's a bit cluttered

301
00:12:43,967 --> 00:12:46,133
and it could get
really noisy in here.

302
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:48,900
But the people here are kind.

303
00:12:48,933 --> 00:12:51,367
Just don't do them wrong.

304
00:12:51,367 --> 00:12:54,767
I'm so sorry too about
all the people that could get...

305
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,867
[WHISPERS] gossipy.

306
00:12:57,667 --> 00:13:00,167
Are they talking about me?

307
00:13:00,167 --> 00:13:03,733
Oh, oh, oh, not really.
Not really.

308
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:05,400
That's just the way they are.

309
00:13:06,367 --> 00:13:08,367
Oh, Gloria,
don't worry about it too much.

310
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:11,133
No one would even dare
with Gabo around.

311
00:13:11,133 --> 00:13:13,067
Everyone here is scared of him.

312
00:13:13,067 --> 00:13:15,300
If there's someone
who would dare fight with you,

313
00:13:16,233 --> 00:13:17,300
there's just one person.

314
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,167
Who?

315
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:20,200
Betchay.

316
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:26,667
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

317
00:13:26,667 --> 00:13:28,133
Have they found Sam?

318
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:32,200
They still haven't.

319
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:35,533
I know that they already have
their own lives and careers.

320
00:13:35,533 --> 00:13:36,700
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

321
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:38,533
But as a mother,

322
00:13:38,533 --> 00:13:42,000
I still want to protect them
all the time.

323
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,067
[ISOBEL SOBS]

324
00:13:43,067 --> 00:13:44,500
And now that Sam is missing,

325
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:46,533
I don't know what else to do.

326
00:13:47,167 --> 00:13:48,133
Isobel...

327
00:13:48,733 --> 00:13:51,333
I'm sure Sam is okay.

328
00:13:51,967 --> 00:13:53,967
I am starting to think

329
00:13:53,967 --> 00:13:58,633
that I'm not going to see
the light in this dark

330
00:13:58,667 --> 00:14:00,667
for a long time.

331
00:14:00,667 --> 00:14:03,167
I don't know who else
I can turn to.

332
00:14:04,133 --> 00:14:06,367
I know Sam.

333
00:14:06,367 --> 00:14:08,500
If she's in danger right now,

334
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,867
she'll find someone
who can help her.

335
00:14:10,867 --> 00:14:12,500
I'm sure of that.

336
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:14,567
[DOOR OPENS]

337
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:17,967
Isobel, Ricardo's here.

338
00:14:19,033 --> 00:14:21,133
Ricardo, any updates?

339
00:14:21,133 --> 00:14:23,000
What happened?
Have you found Sam?

340
00:14:24,233 --> 00:14:25,633
Not yet.

341
00:14:25,633 --> 00:14:26,867
Where were you?

342
00:14:27,633 --> 00:14:28,833
Did you go to the Zafras?

343
00:14:30,433 --> 00:14:31,967
[MUSIC TURNS MOROSE]

344
00:14:31,967 --> 00:14:34,033
Did they do this?

345
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,233
Just leave it to me.

346
00:14:42,267 --> 00:14:45,400
I'm doing everything I can
to find Sam.

347
00:14:46,433 --> 00:14:47,833
[ISOBEL BREATHES SHARPLY]

348
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:49,833
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

349
00:14:49,833 --> 00:14:55,567
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

350
00:14:55,567 --> 00:14:57,267
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC
PLAYING ON VIDEO]

351
00:14:57,267 --> 00:14:59,267
That was cool, man! [CHUCKLES]

352
00:14:59,967 --> 00:15:02,400
You were something else there!

353
00:15:02,433 --> 00:15:04,233
- Definitely! [HIGH FIVES]
- That was badass.

354
00:15:04,233 --> 00:15:06,233
Did you see how I projected?

355
00:15:06,233 --> 00:15:08,733
- And the voice modulations too.
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

356
00:15:08,733 --> 00:15:11,733
High pitch, low pitch,
then I did a deeper voice.

357
00:15:11,733 --> 00:15:12,933
- The Vindicator! Oh!
- [DOOR OPENS]

358
00:15:12,933 --> 00:15:14,000
Salvador!

359
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,533
Did you hear

360
00:15:15,533 --> 00:15:18,000
that our ratings
consistently get better?

361
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,833
Especially when it's about
General Jacinto and the NLEA.

362
00:15:21,833 --> 00:15:24,200
They keep failing
at doing their jobs.

363
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,800
I'll critique them all I want.

364
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,933
But the thing is, we haven't
gotten close to General Jacinto.

365
00:15:28,933 --> 00:15:33,400
But once we do,
we'll get better stories.

366
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,933
Our ratings
will probably skyrocket.

367
00:15:35,967 --> 00:15:37,200
The question is...

368
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,767
- [MUSIC TURNS PENSIVE]
- [TONGUE CLICKS]

369
00:15:38,767 --> 00:15:40,600
- how?
- Boss.

370
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:43,700
- Do you remember The Tiger?
- Okay?

371
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:46,233
Agent Jacinto,

372
00:15:46,233 --> 00:15:49,000
who's the daughter
of General Jacinto,

373
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,067
handled The Tiger's case.

374
00:15:51,067 --> 00:15:53,167
- Right.
- Exactly!

375
00:15:53,167 --> 00:15:54,700
- That's smart.
- Well...

376
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:56,167
Of course. [HIGH FIVES]

377
00:15:56,167 --> 00:16:00,033
We will go through Sam Jacinto

378
00:16:00,033 --> 00:16:03,033
to get close to his dad,
Ricardo Jacinto.

379
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:04,167
That's right.

380
00:16:04,167 --> 00:16:05,333
Perfect!

381
00:16:07,833 --> 00:16:08,800
[OBJECT THUDS]

382
00:16:08,833 --> 00:16:10,200
Ricardo, I know you well.

383
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:13,067
I know there's something
you're keeping from me.

384
00:16:13,067 --> 00:16:14,367
Where's my daughter?

385
00:16:14,367 --> 00:16:15,367
Isobel.

386
00:16:15,367 --> 00:16:17,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,967
Don't make this hard.

388
00:16:17,967 --> 00:16:20,800
I want to know the truth!

389
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,767
Where is my daughter?!

390
00:16:22,767 --> 00:16:24,933
I am the former chief of NLEA.

391
00:16:24,933 --> 00:16:26,733
I'm doing my very best
to resolve this,

392
00:16:26,733 --> 00:16:29,700
better than the most important
case I've handled then!

393
00:16:30,767 --> 00:16:32,333
[ISOBEL HUFFS]

394
00:16:32,333 --> 00:16:34,233
Then where the hell is Sam?!

395
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:35,767
If you're doing everything,

396
00:16:35,767 --> 00:16:37,733
then you should've found her
by now!

397
00:16:38,433 --> 00:16:40,600
You're a general,
for Pete's sake!

398
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,333
Do you think I like this?

399
00:16:47,833 --> 00:16:50,833
It's an embarrassment
that my own daughter

400
00:16:50,833 --> 00:16:52,167
is a victim of a crime!

401
00:16:52,167 --> 00:16:53,500
Here we go again.

402
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,567
It's always about you first

403
00:16:57,567 --> 00:16:59,200
instead of your own daughter!

404
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,233
[ISOBEL BREATHES SHARPLY]

405
00:17:02,233 --> 00:17:06,800
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

406
00:17:09,167 --> 00:17:11,633
Rudy, babes,
I'll stay at the back for now,

407
00:17:11,767 --> 00:17:14,167
and keep an eye
on what Elton's doing.

408
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,100
- Alright, alright, alright.
- Alright.

409
00:17:16,267 --> 00:17:18,167
Don't climb up, okay?
The roof's too fragile.

410
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:20,167
- [KULAS] Rudy! Rudy!
- Hey, Kulas!

411
00:17:21,133 --> 00:17:22,100
[KULAS] Hey, Rudy.

412
00:17:22,233 --> 00:17:23,933
Gloria just arrived,

413
00:17:24,067 --> 00:17:26,200
and you immediately had
the roof repaired.

414
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,100
Life is really different
when you have a daughter-in-law.

415
00:17:29,233 --> 00:17:32,700
Hey! What are you saying, Kulas?
I heard that.

416
00:17:32,833 --> 00:17:35,967
Our roof should've been replaced
a long time ago.

417
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:38,067
Gabo got his paycheck

418
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,767
that's why we're repairing
our roof.

419
00:17:40,367 --> 00:17:42,200
It just so happened
that Gloria's here.

420
00:17:42,333 --> 00:17:44,367
[DIDAY]
That's just how it is, Rudy.

421
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,233
You have a beautiful
daughter-in-law.

422
00:17:46,367 --> 00:17:48,633
She needs to feel comfortable.

423
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:50,700
Right, buddy? I mean, Gloria.

424
00:17:51,367 --> 00:17:54,467
But, Gloria,
you have to keep an eye on Gabo!

425
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,533
A lot of girls
are chasing after him!

426
00:17:56,667 --> 00:18:00,467
Look at my husband.
He always disappears at night.

427
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:03,500
I think he wants me
to get back in the slammer.

428
00:18:03,633 --> 00:18:05,300
[KULAS] What are you
talking about, Diday?

429
00:18:05,433 --> 00:18:08,367
But it's true!
You disappeared last night!

430
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:10,133
Kanor and I just went out
for drinks.

431
00:18:10,267 --> 00:18:13,533
See? That's what every man says.

432
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,833
So, Gloria...

433
00:18:16,967 --> 00:18:19,700
Keep an eye on Gabo.
He's always going out.

434
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:23,600
- He's always going out?
- O-Oh my.

435
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:25,667
This conversation
is going nowhere.

436
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,100
You should go back
to your store.

437
00:18:27,233 --> 00:18:28,333
- No one's there.
- Alright, go.

438
00:18:28,467 --> 00:18:30,200
You won't get rich
from gossiping!

439
00:18:30,333 --> 00:18:32,033
- Go on.
- This is what I was saying.

440
00:18:32,167 --> 00:18:33,233
I'm sorry, Gloria.

441
00:18:33,367 --> 00:18:36,700
It'd be better
if we went back inside.

442
00:18:36,833 --> 00:18:40,300
- Let's go.
- Can I stay here for now?

443
00:18:41,067 --> 00:18:42,267
I just need some air.

444
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:43,800
I'll go looking around, too.

445
00:18:43,933 --> 00:18:46,967
Something might trigger
my memories.

446
00:18:49,467 --> 00:18:50,533
Sure!

447
00:18:50,667 --> 00:18:53,100
But don't go too far from here.

448
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:57,067
- Let's go, Mameng.
- Alright, alright.

449
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:58,800
Gloria, stay in this area, okay?

450
00:18:58,933 --> 00:19:01,467
- We'll wait for you inside.
- Yes, yes.

451
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:07,333
[RUDY] Mameng,
I'll go check Gabo's room.

452
00:19:07,467 --> 00:19:08,433
Okay, okay.

453
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:12,233
[ROOF CLANGING]

454
00:19:12,367 --> 00:19:14,600
- Are you okay up there?
- We're doing okay.

455
00:19:14,733 --> 00:19:16,800
- Your roof's too old.
- Be careful!

456
00:19:16,933 --> 00:19:19,400
[ROOF CLANGING]

457
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,267
- Rudy.
- Mameng.

458
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:29,167
Do you think it's okay
that we left Gloria outside?

459
00:19:29,733 --> 00:19:31,767
Who knows where she might go?

460
00:19:31,900 --> 00:19:35,067
Maybe it's better
that she stays here inside.

461
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,867
Let her be.

462
00:19:37,733 --> 00:19:42,600
She might think we're caging her
inside this house.

463
00:19:42,733 --> 00:19:43,833
[THERMOS THUDS]

464
00:19:43,967 --> 00:19:49,367
Rudy, I'm just worrying about
her safety.

465
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:51,300
Didn't you see?

466
00:19:51,433 --> 00:19:53,800
There are still strangers
lurking around!

467
00:19:53,933 --> 00:19:55,467
Look, there's so many people!

468
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:59,467
I'm sure no one
will harm Gloria.

469
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:00,967
Remember last night?

470
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:04,267
Just one shout from Gabo,
and everyone ran out to fight.

471
00:20:04,433 --> 00:20:08,333
But we can't control
every single one of them!

472
00:20:08,467 --> 00:20:11,267
Not everyone knows about Gloria.

473
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:14,167
No matter, just let her be.

474
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:17,133
And it might even help her
regain her memory.

475
00:20:17,267 --> 00:20:18,700
That's another thing, Rudy.

476
00:20:18,833 --> 00:20:22,967
What if she does regain
her memory?

477
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:24,233
We might become the bad guys

478
00:20:24,367 --> 00:20:27,767
for not being able to take care
of that woman properly.

479
00:20:28,367 --> 00:20:31,333
I think Gabo already knows
how that will unfold.

480
00:20:31,467 --> 00:20:33,200
But then again, who knows?

481
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:37,933
She might even thank Gabo
for protecting her.

482
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:39,533
No matter!

483
00:20:40,133 --> 00:20:42,833
That woman should never be
out of your sight.

484
00:20:42,967 --> 00:20:44,367
You have to keep
a close eye on her.

485
00:20:45,100 --> 00:20:46,133
You're unbelievable.

486
00:20:46,767 --> 00:20:49,500
Fine. Look at me.
I won't let her out of my sight.

487
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:53,400
- Is this good enough?
- You really are something!

488
00:20:53,533 --> 00:21:00,500
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

489
00:21:01,833 --> 00:21:08,767
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

490
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,000
- Miss.
- Yes?

491
00:21:16,133 --> 00:21:18,267
Can I get these banana cues?

492
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,567
- How many?
- Four.

493
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,200
- Four pieces of<i> turon too.
</i>- Sure.

494
00:21:21,333 --> 00:21:23,700
And six pieces of corn.

495
00:21:23,833 --> 00:21:25,500
- How much is everything?
- 200 pesos.

496
00:21:25,633 --> 00:21:27,267
That's expensive.
Can't it be 150 pesos?

497
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:29,733
- This is my first sale today.
- Alright, here.

498
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:32,033
For good luck.

499
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:35,100
You're my first customer.
I hope you bring me good luck.

500
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:44,000
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

501
00:21:46,533 --> 00:21:48,500
[DIDAY]
Gloria! Gloria, come here!

502
00:21:48,633 --> 00:21:50,633
Let's drink! Come here, sit!

503
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,767
[ESTONG]
Ma, it's embarrassing for Gabo.

504
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:54,233
Why?

505
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:56,200
- It's not!
- It is!

506
00:21:56,333 --> 00:21:57,800
- Sit here, dear. Sit.
- [SAM CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

507
00:21:58,933 --> 00:22:01,733
- What would you like to drink?
- Anything is fine.

508
00:22:02,333 --> 00:22:05,000
Simang! Get me two beers!

509
00:22:05,133 --> 00:22:06,867
[ESTONG]
Ma, you're giving her two?

510
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,933
Of course! It'd be embarrassing
for our visitor.

511
00:22:09,067 --> 00:22:11,633
- What's with you? That's okay!
- [KULAS] Diday!

512
00:22:11,767 --> 00:22:14,533
You might start saying things
about Gabo again.

513
00:22:14,700 --> 00:22:16,533
What do you mean?

514
00:22:16,667 --> 00:22:19,600
Everything Gabo has done here
is for our good!

515
00:22:20,167 --> 00:22:21,033
[SAM EXHALES]

516
00:22:21,167 --> 00:22:23,700
It's fine. How are you?

517
00:22:23,833 --> 00:22:26,333
[DIDAY]
We're doing fine, Gloria.

518
00:22:26,467 --> 00:22:28,133
It's nice you went out,

519
00:22:28,267 --> 00:22:30,533
so you can get to know
the people here.

520
00:22:30,667 --> 00:22:33,067
[KULAS] Gloria, you have
to excuse my wife.

521
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:35,133
- She's too chatty.
- [SAM CHUCKLES]

522
00:22:35,267 --> 00:22:38,467
It's fine. I want to get
to know you too.

523
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:42,000
And I also want to know more
about my husband.

524
00:22:42,133 --> 00:22:44,767
Gabo? He's my childhood friend.

525
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:46,833
We've been together
since we were kids.

526
00:22:46,967 --> 00:22:48,533
He likes getting into fights
a lot,

527
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:51,133
but he's a very kind man.

528
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:54,333
[KULAS] It's true.

529
00:22:54,467 --> 00:22:56,200
They've known each other
since they were kids.

530
00:22:56,333 --> 00:22:58,433
Gabo was his protector.

531
00:22:59,667 --> 00:23:03,067
[DIDAY]
Here at Ginintuang Lupa...

532
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:08,000
Gabo is our protector.

533
00:23:08,533 --> 00:23:13,667
Not just anyone
can enter here at Paradise.

534
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:16,567
We'd know right away
if a stranger is here.

535
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:21,133
You're very lucky, you know?
Gabo brought you here.

536
00:23:22,067 --> 00:23:25,567
[KULAS] You know, Gloria,
Gabo has good taste!

537
00:23:26,367 --> 00:23:29,767
[DIDAY] What do you mean?
That you don't have good taste?

538
00:23:30,567 --> 00:23:31,733
Huh?!

539
00:23:31,867 --> 00:23:33,233
Remember this.

540
00:23:33,367 --> 00:23:36,600
Don't ever cheat on me!
If I catch you--

541
00:23:36,733 --> 00:23:39,200
[ESTONG] Ma!
It's embarrassing for Gloria.

542
00:23:39,333 --> 00:23:41,400
- Consider our visitor.
- That's enough!

543
00:23:41,533 --> 00:23:44,367
- Stop.
- Yes, don't argue.

544
00:23:45,167 --> 00:23:47,100
- [ESTONG] That's enough!
- [DIDAY] Gloria--

545
00:23:47,233 --> 00:23:49,667
[SELLER] Our polo shirts
are new, handsome!

546
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:52,467
[GABO]<i> Oh, yeah.
</i> It's Papa's birthday tomorrow.

547
00:23:53,067 --> 00:23:54,333
<i> I should buy him a new shirt.</i>

548
00:23:55,467 --> 00:23:58,333
[SELLER] Go buy, handsome!

549
00:23:58,967 --> 00:24:00,900
- Miss, how much is this?
- I'll give it for 200 pesos.

550
00:24:01,033 --> 00:24:03,300
- This one?
- That's all 200 pesos.

551
00:24:04,133 --> 00:24:06,200
I'll buy this.
It's my gift to my father.

552
00:24:06,333 --> 00:24:07,567
Can't you sell it for 180 pesos?

553
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:09,800
- 180 pesos?
- Yes.

554
00:24:10,467 --> 00:24:12,100
Alright, handsome!

555
00:24:12,233 --> 00:24:14,167
- It's 'cause you're handsome.
- Thank you!

556
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:19,233
Gloria, you want some snacks?
You can get from there.

557
00:24:19,367 --> 00:24:20,800
They're all different.
Go on, dear.

558
00:24:20,933 --> 00:24:22,433
- Alright, I'll check it out.
- [DIDAY] Sure.

559
00:24:22,567 --> 00:24:23,767
[ESTONG] We're sorry Gloria.

560
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:27,400
- Don't be scared of Diday.
- [SAM CHUCKLES]

561
00:24:27,533 --> 00:24:29,433
- Okay.
- You're too stubborn.

562
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:36,533
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

563
00:24:40,933 --> 00:24:42,233
You're so pretty.

564
00:24:42,367 --> 00:24:44,500
Are you Gabo's wife?

565
00:24:44,633 --> 00:24:46,200
Oh, thank you.

566
00:24:46,333 --> 00:24:47,567
Yes, I am Gabo's wife.

567
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:49,567
Choose anything you want.

568
00:24:49,700 --> 00:24:50,833
On the house.

569
00:24:50,967 --> 00:24:52,733
Oh, you don't have to.

570
00:24:52,867 --> 00:24:54,333
You can sell them
instead of giving them to me.

571
00:24:54,467 --> 00:24:58,133
- I'm okay.
- Go ahead. For you and Gabo.

572
00:24:59,733 --> 00:25:00,767
Uh...

573
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:03,200
- Take your pick.
- Okay.

574
00:25:04,433 --> 00:25:06,433
Which one's good?

575
00:25:06,567 --> 00:25:08,333
All of them.

576
00:25:09,667 --> 00:25:11,267
Okay. I'll take these.

577
00:25:11,933 --> 00:25:13,333
Is that all?

578
00:25:13,467 --> 00:25:15,333
Okay.
We'll cook these for you.

579
00:25:15,467 --> 00:25:17,533
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

580
00:25:17,667 --> 00:25:19,633
For your wife?

581
00:25:19,767 --> 00:25:21,433
Yes, ma'am.
Does it look nice?

582
00:25:21,567 --> 00:25:23,733
Yes, sir.
You must have a beautiful wife.

583
00:25:23,867 --> 00:25:25,733
- I sure do.
- You should get it, sir.

584
00:25:25,867 --> 00:25:27,233
- It's only 30 pesos.
- How much?

585
00:25:27,367 --> 00:25:29,233
- 30 pesos?
- This one's 50.

586
00:25:29,367 --> 00:25:30,833
- Okay.
- I'll wrap that up for you.

587
00:25:30,967 --> 00:25:32,467
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

588
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:36,567
Thank you.

589
00:25:36,700 --> 00:25:43,700
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

590
00:25:47,467 --> 00:25:48,900
Hey, Gloria!

591
00:25:49,033 --> 00:25:51,233
Do you want me
to fetch you water?

592
00:25:51,367 --> 00:25:52,733
I'd be glad to.

593
00:25:53,633 --> 00:25:55,900
Really?
How much does it cost?

594
00:25:56,033 --> 00:25:59,267
It's very cheap.
10 pesos per container.

595
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,633
10 pesos per container?

596
00:26:01,767 --> 00:26:03,900
Where do you get the water?

597
00:26:04,033 --> 00:26:05,633
We all use
the same water source here,

598
00:26:05,767 --> 00:26:07,400
but you have to wait your turn.

599
00:26:07,533 --> 00:26:10,933
If you get water yourself,
it might take a while.

600
00:26:11,100 --> 00:26:14,267
So we'll fetch it for you,
Gloria.

601
00:26:14,400 --> 00:26:15,967
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

602
00:26:16,100 --> 00:26:18,733
- We got this.
- Okay. Thank you.

603
00:26:18,867 --> 00:26:20,633
- Okay.
- All right, Gloria.

604
00:26:20,767 --> 00:26:21,833
[IN UNISON]
Gloria! Gloria!

605
00:26:21,967 --> 00:26:24,433
We'll fetch you water!

606
00:26:24,567 --> 00:26:25,933
[CHUCKLES] All right.

607
00:26:26,067 --> 00:26:26,833
[WOMAN 1] Gloria!

608
00:26:26,967 --> 00:26:28,233
Do you need help
with your laundry?

609
00:26:28,367 --> 00:26:30,267
I can do it for
you and Gabo.

610
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,533
[SAM] I'll tell him.

611
00:26:31,667 --> 00:26:32,733
All right. Thanks.

612
00:26:32,867 --> 00:26:33,600
[WOMAN 2] Gloria!

613
00:26:33,733 --> 00:26:35,000
Come here!

614
00:26:35,133 --> 00:26:37,400
Here's some
water spinach and string beans.

615
00:26:37,533 --> 00:26:38,833
For you and Gabo.

616
00:26:38,967 --> 00:26:41,200
Wait, let me add more greens.

617
00:26:41,333 --> 00:26:43,633
Oh, you don't have to
do that.

618
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:45,567
It's my pleasure, dear.

619
00:26:45,700 --> 00:26:47,633
Consider it my gift to you.

620
00:26:47,767 --> 00:26:48,700
Oh my...

621
00:26:48,833 --> 00:26:50,667
You're too kind.
Thank you.

622
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:52,333
Don't mention it.

623
00:26:52,467 --> 00:26:57,967
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

624
00:26:58,100 --> 00:27:00,967
[OIL SIZZLING]

625
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:05,133
Hey, how much for this?

626
00:27:05,267 --> 00:27:06,767
50 pesos, Gabo.

627
00:27:09,267 --> 00:27:11,033
Can you do 40?
That's all I have.

628
00:27:11,167 --> 00:27:12,600
Sure, Gabo.

629
00:27:12,733 --> 00:27:14,133
[CHUCKLES]

630
00:27:14,267 --> 00:27:15,967
I want my wife to try it.

631
00:27:16,133 --> 00:27:17,400
Since when did you
have a wife?

632
00:27:17,533 --> 00:27:19,367
- Just yesterday.
- Wow, congrats.

633
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:22,233
- Smells good.
- She'll like that.

634
00:27:26,867 --> 00:27:30,167
Another one?
Seriously?

635
00:27:30,300 --> 00:27:31,933
[GOON 1] Look everywhere!

636
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:34,467
We need to find that woman!

637
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:35,633
- You look over there!
- [GOON 2] Okay.

638
00:27:35,767 --> 00:27:36,967
[GOON 1] You look there!

639
00:27:37,100 --> 00:27:44,067
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

640
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:02,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

641
00:28:05,233 --> 00:28:08,033
[ELTON] Badong is unbelievable!

642
00:28:08,167 --> 00:28:10,833
I told him to bring
everything we need,

643
00:28:10,967 --> 00:28:12,600
but he still forgot
the sealant.

644
00:28:12,733 --> 00:28:14,933
We needed that
to fix the roof.

645
00:28:17,133 --> 00:28:18,167
Here it is.

646
00:28:18,867 --> 00:28:20,833
Can I ask you a question?

647
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,233
Oh, Gloria.
What can I do for you?

648
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:27,133
Is this Gabo's motorcycle?

649
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:30,233
No. This isn't Gabo's.

650
00:28:30,367 --> 00:28:32,200
Rudy had me fix it up.

651
00:28:32,333 --> 00:28:34,567
This belongs to a seaman.

652
00:28:34,700 --> 00:28:38,533
The owner was supposed to
take it back already,

653
00:28:38,667 --> 00:28:40,067
but Gabo used it.

654
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:41,733
He totally wrecked it.

655
00:28:41,867 --> 00:28:44,933
The owner was furious.

656
00:28:45,067 --> 00:28:47,833
He wanted to sue Gabo and me.

657
00:28:49,133 --> 00:28:52,633
Do you know what
Gabo used this for?

658
00:28:52,767 --> 00:28:55,000
I have no idea
where he went

659
00:28:55,133 --> 00:28:57,567
or what he used it for.

660
00:28:57,733 --> 00:29:00,433
You should talk to Gabo,
Gloria.

661
00:29:00,567 --> 00:29:03,300
He always causes Rudy trouble.

662
00:29:03,433 --> 00:29:06,467
Does Gabo use this
for illegal activities?

663
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:08,133
Illegal activities?

664
00:29:08,267 --> 00:29:09,533
I don't think so.

665
00:29:09,667 --> 00:29:14,167
He's changed since
being released from prison.

666
00:29:14,300 --> 00:29:18,867
Although,
Gabo did go to jail

667
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:22,233
because of...

668
00:29:22,367 --> 00:29:24,033
Django!

669
00:29:24,167 --> 00:29:27,967
Django and his lot
are a bunch of delinquents!

670
00:29:28,100 --> 00:29:30,100
Especially his father, Paquito.

671
00:29:30,267 --> 00:29:35,067
He's the leader of
all illegal activities here.

672
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:37,967
Maybe that's what
he used this bike for.

673
00:29:38,100 --> 00:29:39,500
I don't think so.

674
00:29:39,633 --> 00:29:42,100
Gabo has changed his ways.

675
00:29:42,233 --> 00:29:46,333
He came back here to start anew.

676
00:29:46,467 --> 00:29:50,133
But he can't seem
to stay away from trouble.

677
00:29:50,267 --> 00:29:53,567
It's like
he attracts misfortune.

678
00:29:53,700 --> 00:29:55,100
- Oh...
- Um, Gloria?

679
00:29:55,233 --> 00:29:56,467
We need to fix the roof.

680
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:58,400
- Okay.
- See you later.

681
00:30:00,667 --> 00:30:04,367
[SAM]<i> People here don't know
</i> about your illegal activities.

682
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:09,767
<i>I know you use this bike
to commit crimes.</i>

683
00:30:10,733 --> 00:30:13,967
<i>You may be able
to fool your neighbors,</i>

684
00:30:15,867 --> 00:30:18,567
<i> but I see right through you.</i>

685
00:30:21,767 --> 00:30:28,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

686
00:30:44,167 --> 00:30:51,133
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

687
00:31:05,767 --> 00:31:12,733
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

688
00:31:13,300 --> 00:31:16,400
<i>How did the Zafras find out
about Tiger's transfer?!</i>

689
00:31:16,533 --> 00:31:18,333
<i> We almost had Victor!</i>

690
00:31:18,467 --> 00:31:19,600
<i> But they got him back!</i>

691
00:31:19,733 --> 00:31:21,467
<i>- Get inside. It's not safe!
- What?</i>

692
00:31:21,600 --> 00:31:22,667
<i> We're in danger!</i>

693
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:25,000
<i>I saw the men who
were looking for her last night.</i>

694
00:31:25,133 --> 00:31:26,267
<i>They were circling
the basketball court.</i>

695
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:27,633
<i>I saw them
while I was buying food.</i>

696
00:31:27,767 --> 00:31:30,000
<i> We can't let Gloria out.</i>

697
00:31:30,133 --> 00:31:31,633
<i> She's still in danger.</i>

698
00:31:31,767 --> 00:31:33,033
<i> This is all pretend, Gabo.</i>

699
00:31:33,167 --> 00:31:34,900
<i> Don't catch feelings for her.</i>

700
00:31:35,033 --> 00:31:36,900
<i> If she finds out the truth,</i>

701
00:31:37,033 --> 00:31:38,933
<i> she could have you arrested.</i>
